    <name>
      <text>Nested finite collections</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;Use lists to preserve order and sets to ignore order. Here a = \({@a@}\).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Reproduce the nested value \({@[[a,2*x],{1,{2,3}},[]]@}\): [[input:nested]] [[validation:nested]] [[feedback:nested]]&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Reproduce the family of collections \({@{{1,2},[a,2*x]}@}\): [[input:families]] [[validation:families]] [[feedback:families]]&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Reproduce the written form (reorder only) \({@{{x+x,2,2},[1,x+1]}@}\): [[input:form]] [[validation:form]] [[feedback:form]]&lt;/p&gt;</text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;Lists retain order. Nested sets retain their boundaries. EqualComAss also retains written repeated entries and arithmetic form.&lt;/p&gt;</text>
    </generalfeedback>
